# Content and privacy

## Allowed public facts

- Vladislav is 18, a student in the St. Petersburg area, autistic, has ADHD, and is twice-exceptional (2e).
- He builds Discrete Tasks (`https://xgrybvo6508-dot.github.io/discrete-tasks/`), a daily-tasks planner, Idea Pulse, and AI learning systems based on mind maps and interleaving.
- He seeks adult collaborators/cofounders (18–25+) for AI and development projects.
- He prefers direct, concrete text communication, clear expectations, and async work. Respectful questions about autism are welcome.
- His only public contact is X `@VladislavSsqwl`.

Describe projects briefly and do not add private links. Every factual content change belongs in `src/content/profile.ts`; `index.html` may contain only matching preview metadata.

## Voice

Use plain, warm, direct, literal English. Keep claims specific and modest. Do not use hype, idioms, inspirational framing, diagnostic speculation, or pity. Frame “autistic / ADHD / 2e” openly and neutrally-positive.

## Never publish

- email addresses or phone numbers
- exact address or street-level location
- school or university name
- finances
- family information
- health details beyond “autistic / ADHD / 2e”
- secrets, API keys, tokens, private endpoints, or private links

When a requested fact is outside the allowed list, omit it and ask Vladislav rather than inferring it. Run the privacy reviewer before any commit.
